Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 14:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: PS5: a surface's present rectangle is its window's client area.

Every PS5 Vulkan surface is a surface on the display plane (patch 0460), so the host answers
vkGetPhysicalDevicePresentRectanglesKHR with the whole display: 1920x1080 for an ordinary 200x200 window, where Windows
reports the window's client area. Wine's vulkan-1 test checks it (vulkan.c:767, in the created, resized and hidden
contexts, both builds; vulkan-present-mode-122115 on the Pro, 2026-10-27), and it was that test's one console-only
line left. The surface capabilities already report the client area (adjust_surface_capabilities); the present
rectangle now does the same, with the same DPI.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -2410,8 +2410,27 @@
         return VK_SUCCESS;
     }
 
+#ifdef __PROSPERO__
+    {
+        /* Every PS5 surface is a display-plane surface (ps5drv.c), so the host's rectangle is the whole display; Windows
+         * reports the window's client area, as the surface capabilities already do (adjust_surface_capabilities). */
+        VkResult res = instance->p_vkGetPhysicalDevicePresentRectanglesKHR( physical_device->host.physical_device,
+                                                                            surface->obj.host.surface, rect_count, rects );
+        RECT client;
+        if (res >= VK_SUCCESS && rects && *rect_count &&
+            get_surface_rect( surface->hwnd, &client, NtUserGetDpiForWindow( surface->hwnd ) ))
+        {
+            rects[0].offset.x = rects[0].offset.y = 0;
+            rects[0].extent.width = client.right - client.left;
+            rects[0].extent.height = client.bottom - client.top;
+            *rect_count = 1;
+        }
+        return res;
+    }
+#else
     return instance->p_vkGetPhysicalDevicePresentRectanglesKHR( physical_device->host.physical_device,
                                                                    surface->obj.host.surface, rect_count, rects );
+#endif
 }
 
 static void *find_vk_struct( void *s, VkStructureType t )
